     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "As of October 2026, **Iceland’s population is approximately 396,500 people**, according to the latest official quarterly figures I found, published by Statistics Iceland on July 31, 2026. The figure represents the population at the end of June 2026. <Cite refs={[\"turn446501search1\"]}/>\n\n- **Latest official population:** 396,500\n- **Reference date:** June 30, 2026\n- **Population growth:** 1,450 people during the second quarter of 2026\n- **Annual growth:** 1.3% in the year ending January 1, 2026. <Cite refs={[\"turn446501search1\",\"turn446501search0\"]}/>\n\n**Sources**\n\n1. <Entity category=\"organization\" value=\"Statistics Iceland\" disambig=\"Iceland's national statistics office\"/> — [Population in the 2nd quarter of 2026](https://statice.is/publications/news-archive/inhabitants/population-in-the-2nd-quarter-2026).\n2. <Entity category=\"organization\" value=\"Statistics Iceland\" disambig=\"Iceland's national statistics office\"/> — [Population on January 1, 2026](https://www.statice.is/publications/news-archive/inhabitants/population-1-january-2026).\n\n*Note: This is the latest official quarterly figure I found, rather than a real-time population count.*"
     ]
